<section class="band" id="features">
<div class="wrap">
<h2>“Can't I just type in my notes app?”</h2>
<p class="lede">You can. A notes app is for writing things down, though, and Deaftly is for the conversation: the bit where someone's waiting, you're holding your phone up, and they don't know yet that you're deaf.</p>

<div class="feature-grid">
<article class="feature-card">
<span class="mini mini--schemes" aria-hidden="true"><span>Aa</span><span>Aa</span><span>Aa</span></span>
<h3>Type &amp; show</h3>
<p>Type anything and show it full screen in big, clear text. Choose black on white, white on black or yellow on black. If they reply, carry on as a chat.</p>
</article>
<article class="feature-card">
<span class="mini mini--template" aria-hidden="true"><span>Hi! I'm deaf. I'd like a ticket to <mark>Leeds</mark>, please.</span></span>
<h3>Templates</h3>
<p>Messages you use often, ready to go. Tap a highlighted word to change it: pick from a list, type it, or read it off a sign with the camera. Pin your favourites, sort them into categories or write your own.</p>
</article>
<article class="feature-card">
<span class="mini mini--f2f" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mini--f2f__them">I'm collecting a prescription</span><span class="mini--f2f__me">I'm collecting a prescription</span></span>
<h3>Face to face</h3>
<p>Type to someone opposite you while keeping a secure grip on your phone. The keyboard faces you and your words face them, so they read along as you type instead of waiting for the whole message.</p>
</article>
<article class="feature-card">
<span class="mini mini--chat" aria-hidden="true"><span class="bubble bubble--me">Which platform for Leeds?</span><span class="bubble bubble--them">Platform 4, at <b>10:15</b></span><span class="mini__prompt">Your turn – type your reply here</span></span>
<h3>Side by side</h3>
<p>A back-and-forth on one phone, laid out like a script in each person's colour. Clear prompts show the other person where to type. Flip the switch to change turns, and switch sides to match where you're each standing.</p>
</article>
</div>

<div class="camera-block">
<div class="mini mini--menu" aria-hidden="true">
<span>Tomato soup …… 5.50</span>
<span class="mini--menu__picked">Penne arrabbiata …… 11.00</span>
<span>Garlic bread …… 4.00</span>
<span class="mini--menu__add">Add to message</span>
</div>
<div>
<h2>Read text with the camera</h2>
<p>Point your camera at a menu, label, timetable or letter. Tap the lines you want, or drag across words, and add them to your message. You can freeze the picture to make it easier, and turn on the torch when it's dark.</p>
</div>
</div>
